-- title:
--   Level-lattice intersection along a U_ℓ-step
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ be nonzero (the hypothesis being the conjunction $a\neq 0\wedge b\neq 0$) and let $\Lambda_1$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ that is a maximal order in the project's sense: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated and spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and any order containing it equals it. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$. Assume $m$ lies in [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$, the additive subgroup generated by the tensors $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every finite place, that $N\cdot m^{-1}$ lies in the same subgroup, and that the additive group of $R:=\Lambda_1\sqcap\,$[`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $\Lambda_1\,m$ has relative index $N$ in that of $\Lambda_1$. Let $\ell$ be a prime dividing $N$, and let $h$ be a unit belonging to [`CerednikDrinfeld.levelHeckeUSet`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L44) $\Lambda_1\,R\,\ell$, i.e. $h$ lies in `primeHeckeSet` $R\,\ell$ (so $h$ and $\ell\cdot h^{-1}$ lie in the box of $R$, while $h^{-1}$ and $\ell^{-1}\cdot h$ do not), $h$ does not normalise $R$ in the sense that `conjByFiniteIdele` $R\,h\neq R$, and $R\not\leq$ `conjByFiniteIdele` $\Lambda_1\,h$. Then for every unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ the lattices obtained by intersecting $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with the translates of the box of $\Lambda_1$, written [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda_1\,g$, satisfy $$\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda_1\,(xh)\;\sqcap\;\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda_1\,(xm)\;=\;\mathrm{ofFiniteIdele}\,\Lambda_1\,(xhm).$$
--
--   This is the lattice identity governing a Hecke step at a prime dividing the level: for an Eichler-type order $R=\Lambda_1\cap m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}$ of index $N$ in the maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an idele $h$ in the $U_\ell$-set at $\ell\mid N$, the right $\Lambda_1$-lattice attached to $xhm$ is recovered as the intersection of those attached to $xh$ and to $xm$; the exclusion of the ideles that normalise $\widehat R$ or move $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ to an order containing $R$ is exactly what makes the identity hold. It feeds the counting statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.natCard_ofFiniteIdele_levelHeckeUSet_eq_natCard_subgroup_dualPair_ker_of_dvd_of_inf_conjByFiniteIdele`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.natCard_ofFiniteIdele_levelHeckeUSet_eq_natCard_subgroup_dualPair_ker_of_dvd_of_inf_conjByFiniteIdele), where the Hecke action on the class set with level structure at a prime of the level is compared with a kernel of a pairing.
